From: Yu Zhao <yuzhao@google.com>
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] mm: mglru: skip special VMAs in lookaround

Adapted from upstream commit
c28ac3c7eb945fee6e20f47d576af68fdff1392a.

Special VMAs such as VM_PFNMAP can contain anonymous COW pages. Looking
around their PTEs can trigger the pte_special() warning in get_pte_pfn(),
with little reclaim benefit. Skip them as the main page-table walker does.

Adaptation: retain the existing page-based Android 5.15 implementation
and add only the VM_SPECIAL guard. No refactor, vendor hook or ABI change.
The original upstream authorship trailers are retained below; they are
not new sign-offs made on behalf of these contributors.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/c28ac3c7eb945fee6e20f47d576af68fdff1392a
Signed-off-by: Yu Zhao <yuzhao@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -4471,8 +4471,12 @@
 
 	if (spin_is_contended(pvmw->ptl))
 		return;
 
+	/* exclude special VMAs containing anon pages from COW */
+	if (pvmw->vma->vm_flags & VM_SPECIAL)
+		return;
+
 	/* avoid taking the LRU lock under the PTL when possible */
 	walk = current->reclaim_state ? current->reclaim_state->mm_walk : NULL;
 
 	start = max(pvmw->address & PMD_MASK, pvmw->vma->vm_start);
